# These are captured third-party bytes, and their BYTES are the point.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this checkout, so without this every .html and .js
# below would be stored with LF and written back out with CRLF. That is not a
# cosmetic difference here: the corpus is the input to a MEASUREMENT
# (tests/unit/webapi_probe.c), the probe reports byte offsets and script
# lengths, and a page whose script bodies silently grew a byte per line is no
# longer the page that was captured. -text makes git leave them exactly as
# capture.py wrote them, on every platform.
* -text
